ine/godot/pull/110933, but instead of focusing on just one device, I'm implementing a series of virtual devices. These extend an abstracted class called `VirtualDevice` which has properties like multitouch, device index, and visibility functionality (always or touchscreen only). For this to work, I need the engine to have a user-friendly way of telling me the last device used.\r\n\r\nI don't know how to write documents, that's why I asked for an LLM, but since the use of LLM is prohibited, I'm here rewriting the document in the dumbest way possible, but it's the only way I know how to write. I know how to program, not write documents.\r\n\r\nTo do this, what I did was add some return functions directly to the input, as well as a signal output whenever the value changes.\r\n\r\nSorry for not providing a detailed and explanatory text, but due to rules against the use of AI, this is all I can say about the system (I'm neurodivergent, I didn't want to randomly include this in a pull request, but I'm being forced to since people keep complaining about my communication).","labels":[{"id":73330068,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2OA==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/feature%20proposal","name":"feature proposal","description":"","color":"4466ff","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279096997,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTY5OTc=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/archived","name":"archived","description":"","color":"aaaaaa","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":890310664,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw4OTAzMTA2NjQ=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:input","name":"topic:input","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-01-12T13:11:31Z","updated_at":"2026-01-13T02:12:48Z","closed_at":"2026-01-12T15:03:42Z","merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"1bd